module

public import WeilConjectures.TraceFormula.SpaceLineTestMap

/-! # Coefficientwise base change on a single scheme test -/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- Generation and the specified fraction maps commute with coefficientwise base change
on individual scheme tests. This statement constructs neither an open algebraic space
nor a natural transformation.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors on Spaces, Tag 0D2Z(3); Constructions, Tags 01NK
and 01O9 (blueprint: lem-trf-space-line-test-base-change).

Proof: Refine the test by affine opens above affine opens V' and V of the two bases,
and trivialize its line. The graded base-change condition says that each primed
homogeneous piece is generated by scalar multiples of images of unprimed elements.
The specified component equation and linearity identify its scalar images with
those same combinations. In the local ring of a point their generated ideal is the
unit ideal exactly when one unprimed homogeneous image of positive degree is a unit.
This proves equality of the two unions of generator opens; reflection here takes
place in the same local ring, and requires no flatness. For the map comparison,
these generator opens cover a generating test. On such an open, use the coefficient
map D.map to compare the two Proj charts. It sends a degree-zero fraction b/a^m to
D(b)/D(a)^m. The two specified maps evaluate this fraction to the same scalar
image of b divided by the m-th power of the scalar image of a. All elements of the
homogeneous localization have such representatives. The affine adjunction gives
chart equality, and the relative-Proj comparison and scheme gluing give the stated
equality of maps. Refine intersections by affine opens rather than assuming they
are affine. The argument includes arbitrary degrees, zero divisors and empty tests. -/
theorem space_line_test_base_change {S : Scheme.{u}}
    {F G : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {T T' : Over S}
    {f : F ⟶ yoneda.obj T} {f' : G ⟶ yoneda.obj T'}
    {A : T.left.GradedAlgebraData} {A' : T'.left.GradedAlgebraData}
    {L : TestLineFamily F} (hL : L.IsCoherent) (ψ : GradedLineMap f A L)
    (k : G ⟶ F) (g : T' ⟶ T)
    (hcomm : k ≫ f = f' ≫ yoneda.map g)
    (D : Scheme.GradedAlgebraData.PullbackData g.left A A')
    (ψ' : GradedLineMap f' A' (L.pullback k)) (hψ' : ψ.IsBaseChange k g D ψ') :
    (∀ W : SchemeTests G,
      ψ'.generationSet W = ψ.generationSet ((CostructuredArrow.map k).obj W)) ∧
    ∀ (W : SchemeTests G) (hW : ψ'.generationSet W = Set.univ)
      (q : W.left ⟶ projOver T A) (q' : W.left ⟶ projOver T' A'),
      ψ.IsCanonicalTestMap ((CostructuredArrow.map k).obj W) q →
      ψ'.IsCanonicalTestMap W q' → q'.left ≫ D.relProjComparison = q.left := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
